<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Adil Shah II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1672">1672</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> II ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a> from 1656 to 1672. His reign opened with a Mughal invasion under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> and saw the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, who killed the Bijapuri general Afzal Khan in 1659 and carved a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>'s western lands. Bijapur repulsed a Mughal army under Jai Singh in 1665–1666, and the court poet Nusrati wrote major works of Dakhni literature under his patronage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-adil-shah-ii.jpg" alt="Ali Adil Shah II" width="320" height="540" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ali_Adil_Shah_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
